---
name: kickoff
description: Start-of-session routine for the hub workspace — show the brief, run the fast gates, and pick the next unfinished item. Use at the beginning of a session or after /clear. (Named kickoff because /resume is Claude Code's built-in conversation resume.)
disable-model-invocation: true
---

# /kickoff

Before step 1, check that this session runs the hub's hooks and settings: Read `<hub>/.claude/guard_probe.p12`, where
`<hub>` is the absolute path of the directory with `hub.json` (the file does not exist and nothing creates it). Call the
session guarded only if both hold: the result is a denial whose reason contains `[hub guard]` and not `could not check`
(a broken guard's ask also carries `[hub guard]`), and your primary working directory (shown in your environment block)
is `<hub>` itself, because Claude Code loads a project's settings only from the directory the session started in. Then
say so in one line. Otherwise state first, loudly, before the brief, that this session is unguarded (or, when only the
denial holds, that the hub's settings are not loaded), and list what is or may be off: the guard (secrets, force and
default-branch pushes, AI attribution, test-assertion and guarded-path asks), the session brief, the post-edit format
and lint, the stop gate, the pre-compact snapshot, the session-end inbox stub, the attribution settings (no AI co-author
or 'Generated with' lines), and the permission rules and the sandbox. To be guarded, start the session in the hub
directory itself (not in an app repo or a parent directory, and not with the hub attached as an extra directory), then
run `/kickoff` again.

1. Run `./hub brief` (`make brain-brief`) from the hub (the directory with `hub.json`) and show it verbatim. If `AGENTS.project.md` is empty (no project rules yet) or `hub.json` → `repos` has a new repo, one whose `dir` `AGENTS.project.md` does not name, suggest `/onboard` before anything else.
2. Read `brain/now.md` and the newest `brain/journal/YYYY/MM/DD.md`. If a handoff note is referenced there, read it fully.
3. For each repo in `hub.json` → `repos` with local changes, run its `check_fast` command inside the worktree that has the changes
   (never on a stale main checkout). A repo with an empty `check_fast` has no fast gate yet: say so.
4. Check that `git config user.email` in the hub and in each repo equals `hub.json` → `project.author_email`; if it
   differs, say so before any commit. If the session was given a `claude/…` branch (cloud sessions), it is not a repo
   branch: work on `jdoe/{ISSUE}-{slug}` (or the repo's own, `hub.json` → `repos[].conventions`).
5. Propose the next unfinished item (from `now.md` → "Next", the handoff, or open PRs in the brief) and ask before starting; suggest `/fix` for a bug or a small bounded task within `/fix`'s limits (one repo, at most 5 changed non-test files, no new contract, no path under `guard.ask_before_edit`), `/feature` otherwise (create the tracker issue first if there is none).
   An issue that is not ready yet goes to `/triage` first; an open PR to drive to merge, to `/deliver`; someone else's PR, to `/review`.

Never start editing during /kickoff. If `now.md` and the repos disagree (e.g. a PR listed as open is merged), say so.
